            <div xml:id="d574">

                <pb facs="0848" n="734" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg734"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1238: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Paraguay</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Horn</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-26T14:00:00-04:00">June 26, 1931—2
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>22. Your 62, June 25, 3 p.m.<anchor n="69" xml:id="d574-f1"/> Cable text of
                    Bolivian and Paraguayan notes. This matter has been discussed with the neutral
                    representatives in Washington who deplore as does this Government making this
                    matter an incident of such importance that it may threaten suspension of
                    diplomatic relations between Bolivia and Paraguay. Paraguay has been endeavoring
                    to have the Chaco matter discussed with Bolivia in Washington and now that the
                    neutral governments have again taken the matter up and have paved a way for this
                    it would seem to be exceedingly shortsighted to do anything which might prevent
                    the carrying out of the good offices. Please discuss the matter with the
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs and counsel moderation and point out the advantages
                    of adopting a conciliatory attitude so that the negotiations can proceed. Keep
                    the Department fully informed by cable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
